 "section_summary": "This section covers pages 176–239 of an extensive post-World War II survey and institutional directory of educational institutions in Ibaraki Prefecture, Japan. It opens with the final two summary statistical tables of Part Two (Tables 11 and 12), reporting enrollment and teacher numbers for private schools and institutions under other Japanese ministries as of April and November 1946. The remainder forms the beginning of Part Three, a comprehensive institutional roster detailing national, prefectural, municipal, and town/village schools across higher, secondary, and elementary levels, including founding dates, exact locations, and gender-disaggregated counts of students and full- and part-time teachers.",
